  "alias": "Elliot Hilderbrand",
  "publishedDate": "2022-12-14T00:00:00.000Z",
  "score": 90,
  "snippet": "The core of The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt remains unchanged, thank god. It's the same game we all fell in love with before. Playing on a PlayStation 5 and being able to play around with the new controls, including the haptic and adaptive triggers made playing as Geralt all the better. The new quick casting system works wonders for me, and if it doesn't for you then you retain the old configuration. The framerate has been given a noticeable overhaul as well. I no longer chugged about when I ran while in a city full of objects. This is the perfect excuse to play The Witcher 3 again. The best part of the update is that it's completely free; you can't afford not to play again.",
  "title": "The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt Next Gen Review - Gaming Nexus",
  "isQuoteManual": true,
  "medianAtTimeOfReview": 80,
  "npScore": 100,
